  "rationales": {"U":"'selection, qualification and non- exclusion criteria' is a compound noun phrase without definitions or references; users unfamiliar with procurement jargon (e.g., 'non- exclusion criteria') cannot reliably interpret the term without external documentation — evidence: 'selection, qualification and non- exclusion criteria';","A":"'non- exclusion criteria' contains a typographical space ('non- exclusion') that introduces syntactic ambiguity; it may be misread as 'non-exclusion' (correct) or 'non- exclusion' (broken hyphenation), and 'shall include' lacks specification of format, location, or completeness — evidence: 'non- exclusion criteria';","C":"The requirement aligns with common EU procurement directives (e.g., Directive 2014/24/EU Art. 56–57), so correctness is plausible but not verifiably anchored to a cited standard; no source or version is provided — evidence: 'it shall include the selection, qualification and non- exclusion criteria';","V":"No testable condition is specified: no definition of 'includes', no required field names, no structural constraints (e.g., XML element, JSON property, or mandatory text label), and no pass/fail observable outcome — evidence: 'it shall include the selection, qualification and non- exclusion criteria'"},
  "suggestions": {"U":"When a contracting authority publishes a contract notice, it shall include the following three explicitly labeled sections: 'Selection Criteria', 'Qualification Criteria', and 'Non-exclusion Criteria', each containing at least one complete sentence describing the applicable condition;","A":"When a contracting authority publishes a contract notice, it shall include the following three machine-readable, top-level fields in the notice payload: selectionCriteria (string array), qualificationCriteria (string array), and nonExclusionCriteria (string array), each containing at least one non-empty UTF-8 string;","C":"When a contracting authority publishes a contract notice, it shall include the selection, qualification and non-exclusion criteria as defined in Directive 2014/24/EU Article 56(1), Article 57(1)–(4), and Annex V, Part C, respectively;","V":"The contract notice payload SHALL contain exactly three non-empty JSON object properties: 'selectionCriteria', 'qualificationCriteria', and 'nonExclusionCriteria'; each property value SHALL be a non-empty array of strings, and the entire payload SHALL validate against schema v1.2.0 defined in /schemas/notice-contract-2024.json"},
